# --- Server-side only (used by api/token.py, NEVER exposed to the browser) ---
# Get a free key at https://ably.com .
# Use a key with Publish/Subscribe/Presence + token-issuing capability.
#
# Locally: put it in .env (already gitignored) and run with `vercel dev`
# (needed because this project has a serverless function alongside static
# files — plain `python app.py` alone won't route /api/token).
# In production: set it in Vercel's dashboard as an environment variable
# (Project Settings -> Environment Variables) — never commit it.

ABLY_API_KEY=your_ably_key_here
